---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MEDICAID-READY — Medicaid Billing Compliance Kit for Peer Support"
  description="The complete Medicaid billing compliance kit for peer support organizations. Credentialing checklists, documentation templates, consent forms, and billing guidance built for audit-ready operations."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-teal-900 to-slate-900 text-white">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-20 sm:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <span class="inline-block bg-teal-500/20 border border-teal-400/30 text-teal-300 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full mb-6">
          Session Supply Co. — Medicaid Billing Compliance Kit
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight mb-6">MEDICAID-READY</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Stop guessing whether your peer support program is billing Medicaid correctly. This kit gives you the documentation, checklists, and compliance framework to get — and stay — audit-ready.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-400 mb-10">Built for peer support organizations, certified community behavioral health clinics, and recovery programs billing H0038 / H2015.</p>
        <a
          href="https://gumroad.com/l/PLACEHOLDER_MEDICAID_READY"
          class="gumroad-button inline-block bg-teal-500 hover:bg-teal-400 text-white font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded-lg transition-colors text-lg"
          data-gumroad-overlay-checkout="true"
        >
          Get the Kit
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problem Section -->
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Most peer support organizations aren't billing-ready — and don't know it</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          You're delivering real services that change lives. But Medicaid auditors don't evaluate outcomes — they evaluate documentation. A claim that isn't properly supported can be recouped years after it was paid, leaving your organization holding a bill for services you legitimately provided.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          The most common gaps aren't complicated — they're process gaps. Credentialing files that aren't complete. Notes that reference the right codes but not the treatment plan goals. Consent forms that predate 42 CFR Part 2 updates. Supervision ratios that aren't tracked.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          MEDICAID-READY was built to close those gaps systematically, not by reading federal guidance documents, but by having the right tools already designed for your workflow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What's Included -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 text-center mb-3">What's included</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-500 text-center mb-12 max-w-xl mx-auto">A complete compliance system, not just a checklist. Every component is designed to work together.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        {[
          {
            icon: 'M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z',
            title: 'Credentialing Tracker',
            desc: 'Track peer specialist credentials, expiration dates, and renewal requirements across your whole team. Never bill on a lapsed credential.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z',
            title: 'Session Note Templates',
            desc: 'Progress note templates pre-structured to meet Medicaid documentation requirements — treatment plan linkage, duration, and required elements built in.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2',
            title: '42 CFR Part 2 Consent Forms',
            desc: 'Updated consent forms reviewed against 2020 Part 2 amendments. Covers billing disclosures, treatment coordination, and program-specific requirements.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z',
            title: 'Billing Code Reference Guide',
            desc: 'H0038, H2015, and state-specific codes — with place of service requirements, modifier guidance, and common denial reasons mapped to fixes.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z',
            title: 'Supervision Log Templates',
            desc: 'Track supervisory sessions, ratios, and documentation to meet state Medicaid supervision requirements for peer support billing.',
          },
          {
            icon: 'M9 19v-6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v6a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2zm0 0V9a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v10m-6 0a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v14a2 2 0 01-2 2h-2a2 2 0 01-2-2z',
            title: 'Audit Readiness Checklist',
            desc: 'A pre-audit checklist that walks through every documentation requirement so you can identify gaps before an auditor does.',
          },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6">
            <div class="w-9 h-9 bg-teal-50 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-teal-700" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d={item.icon} />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who It's For -->
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">Who this is for</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-4">
            {[
              'Peer support organizations beginning to bill Medicaid',
              'Programs that have received a billing audit or recoupment demand',
              'Operations managers building compliance infrastructure from scratch',
              'Program directors who want confidence before their first Medicaid claim',
              'CCBHCs and behavioral health orgs adding peer support services',
            ].map((item) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-teal-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
                </svg>
                <span class="text-slate-700">{item}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-teal-50 border border-teal-100 rounded-2xl p-8">
          <p class="text-teal-900 font-semibold text-lg mb-3">Ready to get billing-ready?</p>
          <p class="text-teal-800 text-sm mb-6 leading-relaxed">
            The MEDICAID-READY kit is a one-time purchase, instant download. No subscription. No waiting. Everything you need to close your compliance gaps today.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://gumroad.com/l/PLACEHOLDER_MEDICAID_READY"
            class="gumroad-button inline-block w-full bg-teal-700 hover:bg-teal-800 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3.5 rounded-lg transition-colors text-center"
            data-gumroad-overlay-checkout="true"
          >
            Get the Kit
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-20 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 text-center mb-12">Common questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        {[
          {
            q: 'Is this specific to my state\'s Medicaid program?',
            a: 'The kit covers federal requirements and provides a framework applicable across states. It includes a state-specific credentialing reference guide and notes where requirements vary. You\'ll still want to verify your state\'s specific codes and supervision ratios.',
          },
          {
            q: 'We already have some documentation templates. Will this still be useful?',
            a: 'Yes — the value is in having a complete, integrated system. The audit readiness checklist alone has helped organizations identify gaps they didn\'t know existed in documentation they thought was already compliant.',
          },
          {
            q: 'What format are the files?',
            a: 'Templates are provided in Word (.docx) and Google Docs formats so they\'re easy to customize. Tracking tools are in Excel and Google Sheets. The reference guide is a PDF.',
          },
          {
            q: 'Is this a substitute for legal or compliance counsel?',
            a: 'No. The MEDICAID-READY kit is an operational toolkit, not legal advice. For complex compliance questions or active audits, work with a qualified healthcare compliance attorney or consultant. This kit gets your day-to-day operations in order.',
          },
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-2">{item.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm leading-relaxed">{item.a}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
